IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`
IMPORT `oa3-helpers`
IMPORT `oa3-part1-payments`

-- Tests of oa3-part1-payments.l4 (regs 24 to 28.1). Every expected value is worked out by hand from the words of the
-- regulation; each date edge is tested on both sides, and each rule that can answer "not covered" is asked a case that does.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Reg 24(1): the person or agency to whom the Minister may direct the benefit. Evidence of incapacity is the gate; (a) is looked
-- at first and (b) only "where the Minister is not satisfied that any person or agency is so authorized".
-- No evidence of incapacity: nobody under this subsection, whatever else is true.
#ASSERT `reg 24(1): the person or agency to whom the Minister may direct the benefit to be paid on behalf of the beneficiary` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `reg 24(1): No person or agency under this subsection`
-- Evidence, and the Minister is satisfied someone is authorized by law: (a), even though an appointee under (b) also exists.
#ASSERT `reg 24(1): the person or agency to whom the Minister may direct the benefit to be paid on behalf of the beneficiary` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `reg 24(1)(a): a person or agency authorized by or pursuant to a law of Canada or of a province to manage the affairs of the beneficiary`
#ASSERT `reg 24(1): the person or agency to whom the Minister may direct the benefit to be paid on behalf of the beneficiary` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `reg 24(1)(a): a person or agency authorized by or pursuant to a law of Canada or of a province to manage the affairs of the beneficiary`
-- Evidence, nobody authorized, an appointee with an agreement: (b).
#ASSERT `reg 24(1): the person or agency to whom the Minister may direct the benefit to be paid on behalf of the beneficiary` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `reg 24(1)(b): a person or agency the Minister appoints that has entered into an agreement with the Minister to administer and expend the benefit`
-- Evidence, nobody authorized and no agreement: nobody.
#ASSERT `reg 24(1): the person or agency to whom the Minister may direct the benefit to be paid on behalf of the beneficiary` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `reg 24(1): No person or agency under this subsection`

-- Reg 24(2): the duty to furnish directions arises only once a person or agency has been appointed.
#ASSERT `reg 24(2): the Minister must furnish directions regarding the administration and expenditure of the benefit in the best interests of the beneficiary` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 24(2): the Minister must furnish directions regarding the administration and expenditure of the benefit in the best interests of the beneficiary` FALSE)

-- Reg 24(3): the duty to account falls on an appointee; with no appointee there is nothing to account for, so the duty is met.
#ASSERT `reg 24(3): the person or agency has met the duty to account` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 24(3): the person or agency has met the duty to account` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 24(3): the person or agency has met the duty to account` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 24(3): the person or agency has met the duty to account` FALSE TRUE

-- Reg 24(4): the notices of section 25 are given by the person or agency when the benefit is paid to one; otherwise by the beneficiary.
#ASSERT `reg 24(4): the party who must give the notices required by regulation 25` TRUE EQUALS Representative
#ASSERT `reg 24(4): the party who must give the notices required by regulation 25` FALSE EQUALS Beneficiary

-- Reg 24(5): a payment after death goes to the estate, or if there is no estate to the person or agency the Minister designates,
-- where (a) an amount is payable to the deceased or (b) a payment is returned after death.
#ASSERT `reg 24(5): the party to whom a benefit payment may be made after the beneficiary's death` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST Estate
#ASSERT `reg 24(5): the party to whom a benefit payment may be made after the beneficiary's death` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST Representative
#ASSERT `reg 24(5): the party to whom a benefit payment may be made after the beneficiary's death` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST Estate
#ASSERT `reg 24(5): the party to whom a benefit payment may be made after the beneficiary's death` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST Representative
#ASSERT `reg 24(5): the party to whom a benefit payment may be made after the beneficiary's death` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST Estate
-- Neither (a) nor (b): nothing in this subsection permits a payment (not covered).
#ASSERT `reg 24(5): the party to whom a benefit payment may be made after the beneficiary's death` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 24(5): the party to whom a benefit payment may be made after the beneficiary's death` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Reg 25(1): an absence "in excess of one month". Left 2020-01-01: one month after is 2020-02-01, so 2020-02-01 is a month
-- exactly (not in excess) and 2020-02-02 is in excess.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 25(1): the applicant or beneficiary has absented himself from Canada for a period in excess of one month` (YMD 2020 1 1) (YMD 2020 2 1))
#ASSERT `reg 25(1): the applicant or beneficiary has absented himself from Canada for a period in excess of one month` (YMD 2020 1 1) (YMD 2020 2 2)
#ASSERT `reg 25(1): the first day on which the absence is in excess of one month` (YMD 2020 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2020 2 2
-- Left 2020-01-31: one month after clamps to 2020-02-29 (2020 is a leap year), so 2020-02-29 is not in excess and 2020-03-01 is.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 25(1): the applicant or beneficiary has absented himself from Canada for a period in excess of one month` (YMD 2020 1 31) (YMD 2020 2 29))
#ASSERT `reg 25(1): the applicant or beneficiary has absented himself from Canada for a period in excess of one month` (YMD 2020 1 31) (YMD 2020 3 1)
#ASSERT `reg 25(1): the first day on which the absence is in excess of one month` (YMD 2020 1 31) EQUALS YMD 2020 3 1
-- Same left day in a non-leap year clamps to 2021-02-28.
#ASSERT `reg 25(1): the first day on which the absence is in excess of one month` (YMD 2021 1 31) EQUALS YMD 2021 3 1
-- A one-day absence, and one that has not ended before the question day.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 25(1): the applicant or beneficiary has absented himself from Canada for a period in excess of one month` (YMD 2020 5 10) (YMD 2020 5 11))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 25(1): the applicant or beneficiary has absented himself from Canada for a period in excess of one month` (YMD 2020 5 10) (YMD 2020 5 10))

-- The day by which the Minister must be notified of the return: one month after the return, clamped to the end of a shorter month.
#ASSERT `reg 25(1): the last day on which the Minister may be notified of the return` (YMD 2020 1 31) EQUALS YMD 2020 2 29
#ASSERT `reg 25(1): the last day on which the Minister may be notified of the return` (YMD 2020 3 31) EQUALS YMD 2020 4 30
#ASSERT `reg 25(1): the last day on which the Minister may be notified of the return` (YMD 2020 12 15) EQUALS YMD 2021 1 15

-- Both notices given. No absence in excess of a month: no duty, so the notices are given whatever else is true.
#ASSERT `reg 25(1): the applicant or beneficiary has given the notices` FALSE FALSE (YMD 2020 1 31) NOTHING
-- An absence in excess of a month, notice of it forthwith, and the return notified on the last day (2020-02-29): given.
#ASSERT `reg 25(1): the applicant or beneficiary has given the notices` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2020 1 31) (JUST (YMD 2020 2 29))
#ASSERT `reg 25(1): the applicant or beneficiary has given the notices` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2020 1 31) (JUST (YMD 2020 2 1))
-- The day after the last day: not given in time.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 25(1): the applicant or beneficiary has given the notices` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2020 1 31) (JUST (YMD 2020 3 1)))
-- Never notified of the return (not covered by a day): not given.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 25(1): the applicant or beneficiary has given the notices` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2020 1 31) NOTHING)
-- The absence notice was not given forthwith: not given, though the return was notified in time.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 25(1): the applicant or beneficiary has given the notices` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2020 1 31) (JUST (YMD 2020 2 1)))

-- Reg 25(2): the duty to notify of the address, and of any change of it forthwith.
#ASSERT `reg 25(2): the person must notify the Minister of the address to which the benefit is to be sent` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 25(2): the person must notify the Minister of the address to which the benefit is to be sent` FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 25(2): the person must forthwith notify the Minister of a change of the address to which the benefit is to be sent` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 25(2): the person must forthwith notify the Minister of a change of the address to which the benefit is to be sent` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 25(2): the person must forthwith notify the Minister of a change of the address to which the benefit is to be sent` FALSE TRUE)

-- Reg 25(3): joint applicants become separated: the beneficiary AND the pensioner must notify. Reg 25(4): death of the beneficiary: the pensioner.
#ASSERT `reg 25(3): the parties who must immediately notify the Minister of the separation` TRUE EQUALS LIST Beneficiary, Pensioner
#ASSERT `reg 25(3): the parties who must immediately notify the Minister of the separation` FALSE EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `reg 25(4): the parties who must immediately notify the Minister of the death` TRUE EQUALS LIST Pensioner
#ASSERT `reg 25(4): the parties who must immediately notify the Minister of the death` FALSE EQUALS EMPTY

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Reg 26(1): "shall suspend" where it appears the beneficiary is ineligible; "may suspend" where it appears further inquiry is necessary.
#ASSERT `reg 26(1): whether the Minister must or may suspend the payment of the benefit` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `reg 26(1): The Minister must suspend the payment`
-- Both appear: the stronger, "shall", governs.
#ASSERT `reg 26(1): whether the Minister must or may suspend the payment of the benefit` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `reg 26(1): The Minister must suspend the payment`
#ASSERT `reg 26(1): whether the Minister must or may suspend the payment of the benefit` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `reg 26(1): The Minister may suspend the payment`
#ASSERT `reg 26(1): whether the Minister must or may suspend the payment of the benefit` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `reg 26(1): The payment is not suspended under this subsection`
-- A suspension continues until evidence satisfactory to the Minister is given that the beneficiary is eligible.
#ASSERT `reg 26(1): the suspension continues` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26(1): the suspension continues` TRUE)

-- Reg 26(2): the days of the period of suspension for which payment must be made. Suspension 2020-03-01 to 2020-03-31 (31 days).
-- An eligible span wholly inside: 2020-03-10 to 2020-03-14 is 5 days.
#ASSERT `reg 26(2): the number of days of the period of suspension for which the Minister must pay the benefit` TRUE (`Calendar span` WITH `first day` IS YMD 2020 3 1, `last day` IS YMD 2020 3 31) (LIST (`Calendar span` WITH `first day` IS YMD 2020 3 10, `last day` IS YMD 2020 3 14)) EQUALS 5
-- A span starting before the suspension: 2020-02-20 to 2020-03-05 shares 2020-03-01 to 2020-03-05, 5 days.
#ASSERT `reg 26(2): the number of days of the period of suspension for which the Minister must pay the benefit` TRUE (`Calendar span` WITH `first day` IS YMD 2020 3 1, `last day` IS YMD 2020 3 31) (LIST (`Calendar span` WITH `first day` IS YMD 2020 2 20, `last day` IS YMD 2020 3 5)) EQUALS 5
-- A span running past the end: 2020-03-30 to 2020-04-10 shares 2020-03-30 and 2020-03-31, 2 days.
#ASSERT `reg 26(2): the number of days of the period of suspension for which the Minister must pay the benefit` TRUE (`Calendar span` WITH `first day` IS YMD 2020 3 1, `last day` IS YMD 2020 3 31) (LIST (`Calendar span` WITH `first day` IS YMD 2020 3 30, `last day` IS YMD 2020 4 10)) EQUALS 2
-- A span that starts the day after the suspension ends shares nothing: 0 days.
#ASSERT `reg 26(2): the number of days of the period of suspension for which the Minister must pay the benefit` TRUE (`Calendar span` WITH `first day` IS YMD 2020 3 1, `last day` IS YMD 2020 3 31) (LIST (`Calendar span` WITH `first day` IS YMD 2020 4 1, `last day` IS YMD 2020 4 5)) EQUALS 0
-- A span that ended the day before the suspension began shares nothing: 0 days.
#ASSERT `reg 26(2): the number of days of the period of suspension for which the Minister must pay the benefit` TRUE (`Calendar span` WITH `first day` IS YMD 2020 3 1, `last day` IS YMD 2020 3 31) (LIST (`Calendar span` WITH `first day` IS YMD 2020 2 1, `last day` IS YMD 2020 2 29)) EQUALS 0
-- A span of one day on the first day of the suspension: 1 day.
#ASSERT `reg 26(2): the number of days of the period of suspension for which the Minister must pay the benefit` TRUE (`Calendar span` WITH `first day` IS YMD 2020 3 1, `last day` IS YMD 2020 3 31) (LIST (`Calendar span` WITH `first day` IS YMD 2020 2 1, `last day` IS YMD 2020 3 1)) EQUALS 1
-- Eligible throughout: all 31 days.
#ASSERT `reg 26(2): the number of days of the period of suspension for which the Minister must pay the benefit` TRUE (`Calendar span` WITH `first day` IS YMD 2020 3 1, `last day` IS YMD 2020 3 31) (LIST (`Calendar span` WITH `first day` IS YMD 2020 1 1, `last day` IS YMD 2020 12 31)) EQUALS 31
-- Two separate spans: 5 + 3 = 8 days.
#ASSERT `reg 26(2): the number of days of the period of suspension for which the Minister must pay the benefit` TRUE (`Calendar span` WITH `first day` IS YMD 2020 3 1, `last day` IS YMD 2020 3 31) (LIST (`Calendar span` WITH `first day` IS YMD 2020 3 10, `last day` IS YMD 2020 3 14), (`Calendar span` WITH `first day` IS YMD 2020 3 20, `last day` IS YMD 2020 3 22)) EQUALS 8
-- Never eligible, and payment not resumed.
#ASSERT `reg 26(2): the number of days of the period of suspension for which the Minister must pay the benefit` TRUE (`Calendar span` WITH `first day` IS YMD 2020 3 1, `last day` IS YMD 2020 3 31) EMPTY EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `reg 26(2): the number of days of the period of suspension for which the Minister must pay the benefit` FALSE (`Calendar span` WITH `first day` IS YMD 2020 3 1, `last day` IS YMD 2020 3 31) (LIST (`Calendar span` WITH `first day` IS YMD 2020 3 10, `last day` IS YMD 2020 3 14)) EQUALS 0

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Reg 26.1(1): the figure the keel's register (item 11) asks for, six months.
#ASSERT `reg 26.1(1): the prescribed time within which a request for cancellation may be made` EQUALS `a limit in months` 6
-- Payment begins 2020-01-01: six months after is 2020-07-01.
#ASSERT `reg 26.1(1): the last day on which a request for cancellation may be made` (YMD 2020 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2020 7 1
-- Payment begins 2020-08-31: six months after clamps to 2021-02-28.
#ASSERT `reg 26.1(1): the last day on which a request for cancellation may be made` (YMD 2020 8 31) EQUALS YMD 2021 2 28
-- "no later than six months after": the last day is in time, the day after is not.
#ASSERT `reg 26.1(1): the request for cancellation is made in time` TRUE (YMD 2020 7 1) (YMD 2020 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26.1(1): the request for cancellation is made in time` TRUE (YMD 2020 7 2) (YMD 2020 1 1))
#ASSERT `reg 26.1(1): the request for cancellation is made in time` TRUE (YMD 2021 2 28) (YMD 2020 8 31)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26.1(1): the request for cancellation is made in time` TRUE (YMD 2021 3 1) (YMD 2020 8 31))
-- A request on the day payment begins is in time; one made orally is not "in writing".
#ASSERT `reg 26.1(1): the request for cancellation is made in time` TRUE (YMD 2020 1 1) (YMD 2020 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26.1(1): the request for cancellation is made in time` FALSE (YMD 2020 1 1) (YMD 2020 1 1))
-- Reg 26.1(2) and (3): repayment no later than six months after the day the request is granted.
#ASSERT `reg 26.1(2): the last day on which the amount of the pension and related supplement or allowance must be repaid` (YMD 2020 3 15) EQUALS YMD 2020 9 15
#ASSERT `reg 26.1(2): the last day on which the amount of the pension and related supplement or allowance must be repaid` (YMD 2020 8 31) EQUALS YMD 2021 2 28
#ASSERT `reg 26.1(3): the last day on which the amount of the supplement and related allowance must be repaid` (YMD 2020 3 15) EQUALS YMD 2020 9 15
#ASSERT `reg 26.1(3): the last day on which the amount of the supplement and related allowance must be repaid` (YMD 2020 8 30) EQUALS YMD 2021 2 28
#ASSERT `reg 26.1(3): the last day on which the amount of the supplement and related allowance must be repaid` (YMD 2019 8 31) EQUALS YMD 2020 2 29

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Reg 27: the largest amount that may be deducted: the least of the debt, the benefit payable and what avoids undue hardship.
#ASSERT `reg 27: the largest amount that may be deducted and retained out of the benefit` 1000 600 400 EQUALS 400
#ASSERT `reg 27: the largest amount that may be deducted and retained out of the benefit` 1000 600 800 EQUALS 600
#ASSERT `reg 27: the largest amount that may be deducted and retained out of the benefit` 100 600 400 EQUALS 100
-- Undue hardship allows nothing: nothing is deducted. No debt: nothing.
#ASSERT `reg 27: the largest amount that may be deducted and retained out of the benefit` 1000 600 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `reg 27: the largest amount that may be deducted and retained out of the benefit` 0 600 400 EQUALS 0
-- No benefit payable: nothing to deduct from.
#ASSERT `reg 27: the largest amount that may be deducted and retained out of the benefit` 1000 0 400 EQUALS 0
-- Equal figures.
#ASSERT `reg 27: the largest amount that may be deducted and retained out of the benefit` 500 500 500 EQUALS 500

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Reg 28.1(1): all four limbs, and each limb alone broken. Consent signed 2020-03-15: one year after is 2021-03-15.
#ASSERT `reg 28.1(1): the Minister may make a deduction from a benefit` TRUE (YMD 2020 3 15) (YMD 2020 6 1) TRUE 100
-- (b) the record received on the last day of the year (2021-03-15) is "prior to the expiration" of it (fork F-28.1 in NOTES.md); the day after is not.
#ASSERT `reg 28.1(1): the Minister may make a deduction from a benefit` TRUE (YMD 2020 3 15) (YMD 2021 3 15) TRUE 100
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 28.1(1): the Minister may make a deduction from a benefit` TRUE (YMD 2020 3 15) (YMD 2021 3 16) TRUE 100)
-- Signed on a leap day: one year after clamps to 2021-02-28.
#ASSERT `reg 28.1(1): the Minister may make a deduction from a benefit` TRUE (YMD 2020 2 29) (YMD 2021 2 28) TRUE 100
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 28.1(1): the Minister may make a deduction from a benefit` TRUE (YMD 2020 2 29) (YMD 2021 3 1) TRUE 100)
-- (a) no record and consent submitted by the authority.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 28.1(1): the Minister may make a deduction from a benefit` FALSE (YMD 2020 3 15) (YMD 2020 6 1) TRUE 100)
-- (c) no agreement on the procedure.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 28.1(1): the Minister may make a deduction from a benefit` TRUE (YMD 2020 3 15) (YMD 2020 6 1) FALSE 100)
-- (d) the amount deducted "exceeds $50": 50 does not, 50.01 does.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 28.1(1): the Minister may make a deduction from a benefit` TRUE (YMD 2020 3 15) (YMD 2020 6 1) TRUE 50)
#ASSERT `reg 28.1(1): the Minister may make a deduction from a benefit` TRUE (YMD 2020 3 15) (YMD 2020 6 1) TRUE 50.01
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 28.1(1): the Minister may make a deduction from a benefit` TRUE (YMD 2020 3 15) (YMD 2020 6 1) TRUE 0)
-- Received before the consent was signed is still "prior to the expiration" of the year.
#ASSERT `reg 28.1(1): the Minister may make a deduction from a benefit` TRUE (YMD 2020 3 15) (YMD 2020 3 15) TRUE 100

-- Reg 28.1(2): no deduction made, or a deduction for less than might have been paid: the Minister may not authorize any other.
#ASSERT `reg 28.1(2): the Minister is barred from authorizing any other deduction and payment` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 28.1(2): the Minister is barred from authorizing any other deduction and payment` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 28.1(2): the Minister is barred from authorizing any other deduction and payment` TRUE TRUE
-- A deduction made in full: the bar of this subsection does not apply.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 28.1(2): the Minister is barred from authorizing any other deduction and payment` FALSE FALSE)
